SCOPE:
------
When cross-machine receipts diverge, create a minimal reproducible witness:
1. Define "witness bundle" structure:
   - divergence_point (which phase/subsystem failed?)
   - rerun_command (exact command that re-triggers failure on both machines)
   - relevant_inputs (minimal subset of workload that shows divergence)
   - expected_vs_actual (digest comparison showing exact mismatch)
2. Implement witness minimization:
   - Start with full workload
   - Binary-search queries to isolate minimum set that exhibits divergence
   - Document search strategy in WITNESS_MINIMIZATION.md
3. Create witness bundle structure in code (struct definitions)
4. Write unit tests that verify witness bundles parse and can be re-executed

PROOF CRITERIA:
--------------
- Code compiles: `cargo build -p qlever-witness`
- Tests pass: `cargo test -p qlever-witness`
- Witness bundle can serialize/deserialize to JSON roundtrip
- Documentation explains minimization algorithm clearly

DEPENDENCIES:
------------
- qlever-artifact-capture (for receipt format understanding)
- qlever-replay-verifier (for workload replay)
- serde/serde_json (serialization)
- blake3 (digest verification)

INVARIANTS:
----------
- Witness bundles are self-contained (no external state)
- Minimization is deterministic (same input → same minimal witness)
- Witness bundles can be executed standalone
